    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f794795b-ed1e-5936-a17c-a20eae14d6c1",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-28-topic-audit-3/published-probe/17592186096649/d12bd586e3123b80afebf4873fd90c6f19e396447317770c1762683c3337cd86.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the vector $\\mathbf{a}$. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $-2\\mathbf{a}$?",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that $-2\\mathbf{a}$ must be parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nNow, for the vector $-2\\mathbf{a}$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $-2\\mathbf{a}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $-2\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions since the factor $-2$ is negative.\n\nThe required vectors are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-28-topic-audit-3/published-probe/17592186096649/b5e7bae1c7832c93345f0de77dfb18dc2c5b4c9f11dbbf678c5712935da0a804.png)",
